e headword and source opening identify a named person, people, or place. Promotion requires a capitalized whole name and the original article explicitly citing this same BSB verse. No arbitrary qualifier stripping or book-title inference. This citation-constrained rule was reviewed once globally; unmatched contexts remain excluded.","sourceHeadwordId":"Jahaz","term":"Jahaz"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Jahaz","sourceTitle":"Jahaz"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":["Isaiah"],"sourceClass":"profile-title","t":"h"},{"c":["Isaiah was a Judean prophet during the reigns of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah. He was the son of Amoz (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.1.1","r":"Isa.1.1","rawR":"Isa.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.1.1","value":"Isa.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 1:1"},") and was possibly related to King Amaziah. He lived in Jerusalem, was well educated, and had deep insight into human nature. He had a long ministry (about 740~685 BC); as Judah’s political and religious counselor, he had access to kings and was apparently the court historian (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.26.22","r":"2Chr.26.22","rawR":"2Chr.26.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.26.22","value":"2Chr.26.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 26:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.32.32","r":"2Chr.32.32","rawR":"2Chr.32.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.32.32","value":"2Chr.32.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"32:32"},"). Isaiah’s wife was called a “prophetess” (see Study Note on ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.8.3","r":"Isa.8.3","rawR":"Isa.8.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.8.3","value":"Isa.8.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 8:3"},"); their sons were Shear-jashub (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.7.3","r":"Isa.7.3","rawR":"Isa.7.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.7.3","value":"Isa.7.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:3"},") and Maher-shalal-hash-baz (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.8.3","r":"Isa.8.3","rawR":"Isa.8.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.8.3","value":"Isa.8.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"profile-body-fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Isaiah opposed social and political evil at all levels. He censured fortune-tellers. He rebuked kings for their willfulness and indifference. He denounced wealthy, influential people who ignored their responsibilities. And he exhorted everyone to obey God’s covenant. Isaiah opposed Canaanite idolatry and insincere religious observances (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.1.10-17","r":"Isa.1.10-17","rawR":"Isa.1.10-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.1.10-17","value":"Isa.1.10-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:10-17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.29.13","r":"Isa.29.13","rawR":"Isa.29.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.29.13","value":"Isa.29.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"29:13"},"), proclaiming judgment and declaring that only a righteous remnant would survive (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.6.11-13","r":"Isa.6.11-13","rawR":"Isa.6.11-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.6.11-13","value":"Isa.6.11-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:11-13"},"). He foretold the coming Messiah, the peaceful prince of God’s kingdom (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.9.6-7","r":"Isa.9.6-7","rawR":"Isa.9.6-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.9.6-7","value":"Isa.9.6-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:6-7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.11.1-11","r":"Isa.11.1-11","rawR":"Isa.11.1-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.11.1-11","value":"Isa.11.1-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:1-11"},") who was also an obedient, suffering servant (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.53.3-12","r":"Isa.53.3-12","rawR":"Isa.53.3-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.53.3-12","value":"Isa.53.3-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"53:3-12"},"). The book of Isaiah has more overtones of the New Testament than any other Old Testament book and is frequently cited by New Testament authors."],"sourceClass":"profile-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Passages for Further Study"],"sourceClass":"profile-refs-title","t":"h"},{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.19.1-20.19","r":"2Kgs.19.1-20.19","rawR":"2Kgs.19.1-20.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.19.1-20.19","value":"2Kgs.19.1-20.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 19:1–20:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.26.22","r":"2Chr.26.22","rawR":"2Chr.26.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.26.22","value":"2Chr.26.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 26:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.32.20","r":"2Chr.32.20","rawR":"2Chr.32.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.32.20","value":"2Chr.32.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"32:20"},", ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.32.32","r":"2Chr.32.32","rawR":"2Chr.32.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.32.32","value":"2Chr.32.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"32"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.1.1–66.24","r":"Isa.1.1–66.24","rawR":"Isa.1.1–66.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.1.1–66.24","value":"Isa.1.1–66.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 1:1–66:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.3.3","r":"Matt.3.3","rawR":"Matt.3.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.3.3","value":"Matt.3.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matt 3:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.4.14-16","r":"Matt.4.14-16","rawR":"Matt.4.14-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.4.14-16","value":"Matt.4.14-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:14-16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.8.17","r":"Matt.8.17","rawR":"Matt.8.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.8.17","value":"Matt.8.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.12.17-21","r":"Matt.12.17-21","rawR":"Matt.12.17-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.12.17-21","value":"Matt.12.17-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:17-21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.13.14-15","r":"Matt.13.14-15","rawR":"Matt.13.14-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.13.14-15","value":"Matt.13.14-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:14-15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.15.7-9","r":"Matt.15.7-9","rawR":"Matt.15.7-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.15.7-9","value":"Matt.15.7-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:7-9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.1.2-3","r":"Mark.1.2-3","rawR":"Mark.1.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.1.2-3","value":"Mark.1.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mark 1:2-3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.7.6-7","r":"Mark.7.6-7","rawR":"Mark.7.6-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.7.6-7","value":"Mark.7.6-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:6-7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.4-6","r":"Luke.3.4-6","rawR":"Luke.3.4-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.4-6","value":"Luke.3.4-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 3:4-6"},"; ",{"href":